cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DoseCurve in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
title: "DoseCurve: an interactive pharmacokinetics and PK/PD simulator for pharmacy education"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Maati
    given-names: Saif
version: 1.14.0
date-released: 2026-09-30
url: "https://saifmaati.github.io/dose-curve/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Saifmaati/dose-curve"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - pharmacokinetics
  - pharmacodynamics
  - pharmacy education
  - simulation
  - Cockcroft-Gault
  - Michaelis-Menten
abstract: >-
  DoseCurve is a free, browser-based simulator for teaching pharmacokinetics and PK/PD.
  It models one-compartment kinetics (first-order or saturable Michaelis-Menten) for oral,
  IV bolus and infusion dosing with regular, loading, missed and custom schedules, a clinical
  patient with Cockcroft-Gault creatinine clearance, a cited drug library, guided lessons,
  generated practice problems, clinical cases graded by the model, and a public validation
  against an independent solver. It is an educational model, not for clinical dosing.
